MusterFlow turns any API into a typed CLI, an MCP endpoint, and a workflow engine.

Connect:    musterflow connect https://api.github.com
List:       musterflow list
Use:        musterflow swagger-petstore-openapi-3-0 pet find-pets-by-status --status available
Workflow:   musterflow flow create

Usage:
  musterflow [flags]
  musterflow [command]

Available Commands:
  auth        Manage API credentials
  catalog     Community catalog operations
  completion  Generate shell completion script
  config      Manage MusterFlow configuration
  connect     Connect an API from an OpenAPI spec URL or file path
  disconnect  Disconnect an API
  export      Export API registry to JSONL
  flow        Workflow management
  help        Help about any command
  import      Import APIs from a JSONL file
  list        List connected APIs
  mcp         MCP endpoint information
  refresh     Refresh API spec and regenerate commands
  start       Start the MusterFlow dashboard and MCP endpoint
  transform   Manage WASM transforms

Flags:
      --dashboard-addr string       Dashboard HTTP address (default: port from config)
      --data-dir string             Data directory (default: ~/.musterflow)
  -h, --help[=true|false]           help for musterflow
      --no-dashboard[=true|false]   Force local registry mode (skip dashboard detection)
      --output-file string          Output file path (format auto-detected from extension)
  -v, --version[=true|false]        version for musterflow

Use "musterflow [command] --help" for more information about a command.
